        rdfs:label "2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py L1255–L1271" ;
        dcterms:description "Panel I draws the final hybrid state with dense/loose agents over the (u, v) colour render" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L1255-L1271> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Panel I shows an emergent (not templated) adult flank with 4 dark stripes separated by 3 interstripes whose dense iridophores sit in the light bands — the same 4-stripe count the specimen segmentation finds (Panel F, L954-1030) and a plausible rendering of the X0/X1D/X1V sheets of Frohnhöfer 2013 / Singh 2014; Panels E-G keep the SHA-256-locked Danio rerio photograph, its segmented stripes and the standardized profile comparison. Deductions: no juvenile-stage specimen images are vendored, so the 2 -> 4 ontogeny is compared with a qualitative normal table rather than with pictures (-5); dense iridophore coverage of X1D/X1V is sparse compared with the contiguous sheets seen in vivo, and loose iridophores are few (loose fraction 0.02) (-3); the GIF is the model alone with no specimen frame (-2)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): 8-frame growing-flank GIF (SL 7.2 -> 18 mm) with agents and dorsoventral profiles; no juvenile specimen frames — docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_growth.gif: rendered output of 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py at 3aaa03d, image/gif, 387895 B, 1056×440 px, 8 frames, artifact_sha256 2e85b27819c7e94524233f2180f0de10d3ae2797b2ecc37e5725541b68aa02a5 (sha256 2e85b27819c7e94524233f2180f0de10d3ae2797b2ecc37e5725541b68aa02a5), spec_fingerprint 53d32e73f4ffa155070025683029f96e36562f3bf4bf95b4d073d237a096b1d2" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-3> ;
